; A balance assertion naming a lot still matches the lot after a `value`
; expression has been given to it, by a commodity directive (AAPL) or by
; a Value:: tag (MSFT: $100 for 4 units, $25 a unit).
;
; Ledger gives the expression to the lot itself, which every amount of
; the lot shares, and the lot still answers to the name it was bought
; under, so each assertion, which names its lot without the valuation,
; finds the valued lot.  3.4.1 checked a balance assertion against the
; account's holdings stripped of their lot annotations (#2318, #2355),
; so an assertion never found the lot it names, valued or not; here it
; stopped at the AAPL assertion with "Balance assertion off by
; 10 AAPL {$5} [2020/01/01] (({$7})) (expected to see 0)".  It also read
; the tag's $100 as $100 a unit (#2399).

commodity AAPL
    value $7

2020/01/01 Buy
    Assets:Broker    10 AAPL @ $5
    Assets:Cash

2020/01/01 Buy
    Assets:Broker    4 MSFT @ $20  ; Value:: $100
    Assets:Cash

2020/01/02 Check
    Assets:Broker    0 AAPL = 10 AAPL {$5} [2020/01/01]
    Assets:Broker    0 MSFT = 4 MSFT {$20} [2020/01/01]

test bal --lots Assets:Broker
 10 AAPL {$5} [2020/01/01] (({$7}))
4 MSFT {$20} [2020/01/01] (({$25}))  Assets:Broker
end test
